'''Otávia Brito''' (22 August 1932{{Spaced en dash}}5 November 2001) was a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] politician, activist and writer. She rose to confederal prominence during the [[October 76]] events in Balisca, and (as a delegate) later became heavily involved in developing the confederal response to the [[Special Period]]. She went on to win the [[1977 Baliscan premiership election|1977 premiership election]], and upon taking office she became the first [[Ecological Action|Ecologist]] to hold the position. 

Brito, openly [[W:Lesbian|lesbian]], became the world's first [[W:List of the first openly LGBTQ holders of political offices|LGBTQ head of government]] following her election in 1977. 

